// flashcard drill — JAH Roofer Trade Database — What roofers do (jahdb demo program)
var ITEMS=[["What roofers do","Roofers install and repair the weatherproof skin of buildings: asphalt shingles, metal, tile, slate, and flat membranes. It is demanding work at height in all weather \u2014 and one of the best-paid trades for those who maste"], ["Essential tools","Roofing nailer or hammer, utility knife with hook blades, chalk line, tape measure, pry bar, shingle remover, caulk gun, tin snips, and a magnetic sweeper for nails. Safety: harness, rope, and roof anchor \u2014 non-negotiabl"], ["Key skills","Reading the roof: valleys, hips, ridges, penetrations. Proper shingle coursing with correct exposure and nailing. Flashing work \u2014 where roofs actually leak. Tear-off speed and clean deck prep. Estimating squares accurate"], ["Safety essentials","Falls are the leading killer: harness and anchor on anything steep. Heat illness \u2014 hydrate and pace summer work. Tear-off debris: watch below. Power lines near roofs: keep 10 feet. Never work wet or icy roofs."], ["Getting started","Start as a ground helper or tear-off laborer; learn by carrying and watching. Many roofers go independent quickly \u2014 low startup cost. Manufacturer certifications (GAF, Owens Corning) boost credibility and warranties."], ["Pro tips","Flashing details decide whether a roof leaks, not the shingles. Never reuse old flashing. Ice-and-water shield in valleys and eaves. Photograph problem areas for the customer. Clean the yard like a surgeon \u2014 nails in tir"], ["Square","Trade term \u2014 Square: 100 square feet of roofing; the estimating unit."], ["Course","Trade term \u2014 Course: One horizontal row of shingles."], ["Exposure","Trade term \u2014 Exposure: The visible part of each shingle."], ["Valley","Trade term \u2014 Valley: Where two roof slopes meet; a leak hotspot."], ["Ridge","Trade term \u2014 Ridge: The peak where slopes meet."], ["Hip","Trade term \u2014 Hip: The outward corner where slopes meet."], ["Flashing","Trade term \u2014 Flashing: Metal sealing roof